# Change comments

When you change a `.java` or `.pro` file, add a comment on the changed line, or once directly above a contiguous block that is one change. Do not comment unchanged lines.

Use the date of the edit as `YYYYMMDD`.

Java:

```java
// Gary 20261106 - ASC changes: pay flag S is allowed through with a waiver the same as F.
```

Stored procedure:

```sql
-- Gary 20261106 - ASC changes: pay flag S is allowed through with a waiver the same as F.
```

The text after the date starts with `ASC changes:`, then what changed and why. `ASC changes` is the main feature name and belongs on every Java and stored-procedure comment.
